        "original_id": "0f98a054-49b2-57dc-bd68-12d96436a0dd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Franz Liszt, Lord Byron\n- Works: Sardanapale, Sardanapalus\n- Topics: Opera, verse play\n\nFacts:\n- Lord Byron wrote the verse play \"Sardanapalus\" in 1821.\n- Franz Liszt was born on October 22, 1811, and died on July 31, 1886.\n- Franz Liszt was a 19th-century Hungarian composer, virtuoso pianist, conductor, music teacher, arranger, organist, philanthropist, author, nationalist, and Franciscan tertiary.\n- Franz Liszt created the unfinished opera \"Sardanapale,\" cataloged as S.687.\n- \"Sardanapale\" is French for \"Sardanapalus.\"\n- Franz Liszt based \"Sardanapale\" loosely on Lord Byron's 1821 verse play \"Sardanapalus.\"",
